        "headline": "Special Weather Statement issued July 27 at 3:01PM AKDT by NWS Anchorage AK",
        "description": "Daytime temperatures will reach 70 to 75 degrees later this week,\nand will be hottest on Wednesday and Thursday. Temperatures this\nwarm, and for this long, happen about once per year.\n\nThe long duration of warmer days may impact subsistence\nactivities like berry picking, fishing, and hunting. This could\nalso affect people who are extremely sensitive to heat (like\nelders or infants), especially if they are unable to cool down or\nstay hydrated.\n\nActions: Keep homes cool by closing curtains during ",
